# Exact prospective pressure fit

Retrospective source review · fit-fb8ce15096322ec9

Authored interpretation of captured source and receipts. No new training, benchmark, lineage or scientific promotion is implied.

**Method.** A 370,016-parameter linear, bias-free F32 multiscale pressure CNN with one physically scaled residual channel and 19 weight tensors. Two shared neural pressure corrections recompute the F64 sealed cubic-grid equation residual, apply fixed train-only scales and accumulate cell-zero-gauged F64 pressure. Inherited GroupNorm/SiLU labels do not describe its executed linear blocks. It returns pressure, not a physical simulation step; no learned spatial coarse branch is present.

**Purpose.** Qualify a prospective typed pressure fit, exact checkpoint/profile publication and one already-consumed bound field probe.

**Experiment.** 1 CUDA Adam updates, batch one, rate 0.001, model seed 20261015, physical-index seed 2026102501, schedule []. Sixteen physical fitting trajectories/32 frames at 8/16 cells per metre, dt=1/60 s and fluid density 1000 kg/m3. Both manufactured banks and the fixed captured-direction bank remain active; First/final low-spatial-mode feedback weight is 0. The actual entrypoint is typed_pressure_evidence.py; diagnostics use training parents only. The typed evidence wrapper also queries one already-consumed validation frame for publication; it supplies no independent holdout.

**Observed outcome.** Retained train-only final objective 0.26950148549037484; last optimizer loss 573090.35221390729. The three one-update pipeline/prospective/scheduler fits share exact initial and final parameter values. Four prospective outputs missing from its partial local download are freshly verified in the existing native content store using the original receipt hashes; no replacement or copy is created. No fresh common GPU inference, complete simulation-step timing or drift benchmark is added for these fit identities. Historical scheduler/training wall time and normalized diagnostic loss are not deployed latency or worst pressure relative error.

**Lesson.** Keep lifecycle qualification, completed optimizer budgets and scientific accuracy qualification distinct. Repeating an unchanged fit for publication or scheduling can reproduce parameter bytes without creating new scene diversity or an architectural improvement. Byte-equal weights may share retained storage later, but original fit/Run evidence remains separate. A one-update smoke is not a full training result or generalization test.

